        "summary":  "OpenAI released GPT-6 Sol and Luna, complementing the flagship GPT-6 Astra, and cut API pricing by 50% or more: Sol costs $2/$10 per million input/output tokens (down from $4/$20) and Luna costs $0.10/$0.50 (down from $0.20/$1.20). OpenAI attributed the reductions to improvements in caching and inference efficiency. The price cuts apply as standard pricing, not promotional rates.",
        "execSummary":  "OpenAI\u0027s 50% token price cut is a decisive move in the enterprise AI platform war and directly compresses margins for competitors including Anthropic. For enterprise leaders with significant API spend, this changes the ROI calculus on AI workloads and makes previously cost-prohibitive high-volume use cases viable — particularly for customer support automation and document processing at scale. Luna\u0027s $0.10/$0.50 pricing for lighter tasks makes it competitive with open-source deployment costs, raising the bar for self-hosted alternatives. The pace of OpenAI\u0027s model releases — three updates since November 2025 — signals a sustained infrastructure investment advantage that incumbents will struggle to match on price alone.",
        "vendorLean":  "OpenAI — product launch coverage",
        "imageUrl":  null,
        "isNew":  true
