        "summary":  "Microsoft\u0027s HASTE system uses AI to analyze satellite imagery and identify disaster damage within hours rather than weeks. Since 2023, humanitarian organizations have deployed this open-source tool across 23 major disasters in 16 countries to prioritize aid delivery and coordinate search-and-rescue operations. The technology enables responders to make informed resource-allocation decisions when time is critical.",
        "execSummary":  "Microsoft\u0027s HASTE platform compresses post-disaster damage assessment from weeks to hours by applying AI to satellite imagery, and has already been used in 23 major disasters across 16 countries. For enterprise leaders thinking about AI ROI, this is a high-stakes proof point that AI-driven situational awareness at scale is operationally viable today. Organizations in logistics, insurance, and infrastructure should note that the underlying capability — rapid AI-powered geospatial triage — is transferable to supply chain disruptions and risk management. The tool is open-source, lowering the barrier for adoption but also raising questions about governance and accuracy validation.",
