        "execSummary":  "Microsoft Research and two major pharmaceutical firms have produced an AI model that outperforms existing retrosynthesis tools, with expert chemists preferring its outputs 64% of the time — a meaningful bar in a domain where errors cost millions. For enterprise leaders in life sciences or R\u0026D-intensive industries, this signals that multi-model AI architectures are beginning to match or exceed domain-expert judgment on narrow but high-value tasks. The ability to adapt the model to proprietary company data is the key enterprise implication: competitive differentiation through fine-tuned internal AI is becoming realistic. Caveat: lab validation still requires human chemists, and this remains a research result, not a shipping product.",
