        "execSummary":  "Kier Group\u0027s Copilot deployment offers a practical change-management playbook for enterprise AI adoption: grassroots \u0027prompt-a-thons\u0027 converted skeptical executives faster than top-down mandates, and the \u0027Human at the Helm\u0027 framing addressed frontline resistance. For customer-support and operations leaders, the progression from productivity tool to safety-monitoring AI agents mirrors the trajectory most enterprises will follow — starting with productivity wins to fund deeper agentic use cases. The construction context highlights that AI adoption is not confined to knowledge-worker roles; physical operations with high safety stakes are also viable terrain. The article is vendor-produced, so ROI figures should be sought from independent Kier sources.",
