        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s Connected Apps expansion is its answer to the platform consolidation race: by pulling Airtable, Adobe, and others into Gemini via @ mentions, Google is positioning Gemini as the enterprise workflow hub rather than just a chat assistant. For customer-support and operations leaders, this matters because it signals where the industry is heading — AI assistants that orchestrate third-party tools rather than requiring users to context-switch. The implication for enterprise software procurement is real: suites that integrate with major AI platforms will have a distribution advantage over standalone tools. Watch whether Microsoft Copilot connector parity becomes a decision criterion in future M365 renewals.",
