        "summary":  "Six Amazon engineers rebuilt the Bedrock inference engine in 76 days using AI-native development practices — a project originally scoped for 30 developers over 12-18 months. Frontier teams achieve 4.5x to 10x or greater productivity gains by restructuring workflows around AI agents rather than using AI as a coding shortcut. The methodology requires upfront investment in agent context-building and clear requirements before generation begins.",
        "execSummary":  "The productivity numbers here — 30 engineers replaced by 6, timeline cut from 18 months to 76 days — are significant enough to reframe how enterprise technology leaders should be budgeting headcount and delivery timelines. The article\u0027s core argument is that gains are multiplicative only when teams restructure workflows around agents entirely, not when they bolt AI onto existing processes. For customer-support and operations leaders, the implication is direct: centers that redesign workflows around agentic AI will outpace those that add AI as a feature layer. The caveat is that the upfront context-building investment is real and often underestimated.",
