        "date":  "2026-09-17",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Dan Roberts presents seven updated leadership competencies for IT executives navigating the AI era: Coherence, Communication, Currency, Confidence, Conviction, Courage, and Change. These competencies operate within compressed decision timelines and an environment of continuous disruption where speed without alignment produces chaos. Roberts argues these capabilities build on traditional leadership attributes while directly addressing AI-era operating conditions.",
        "execSummary":  "The most decision-relevant point in this framework is the sequencing argument: alignment (Coherence) must precede acceleration, because AI amplifies both good and bad organizational direction equally. For senior leaders managing AI transformation programs, the Currency and Change competencies are particularly high-stakes — staying current on a technology that shifts quarterly while simultaneously managing organizational change fatigue is the defining leadership challenge of this period. The framework is practical for benchmarking your leadership team\u0027s AI readiness beyond technical literacy. The caveat is that frameworks like this tend to be broadly applicable to any technology era; the AI-specific urgency is real, but the underlying leadership principles are not new.",
